      "content": "i get that, but i'm worried if i just use \"loaded language\" it's gonna feel like it's pulling its punches. historical fiction needs to be uncomfortable to be real. if the sheriff is using certain words that were common then, it shows the reader exactly how much power he thinks he has and how much he disrespects the other man. \n\ncan we at least try to draft a version where the sheriff uses the period-accurate, dehumanizing terms? i'm not trying to promote hate, i'm just trying to document the reality of the 1940s for a serious literary work. if i don't include that raw edge, it just feels like a modern story dressed up in old clothes.",
